 create, read, update, delete, search, and count operations",[281,289,290,293,294,298],{},[284,291,292],{},"Full-text search"," - Mark fields with ",[295,296,297],"code",{},"@Text"," to enable full-text search out of the box",[281,300,301,304],{},[284,302,303],{},"Schema evolution"," - Use versioned migration scripts to evolve your data schema safely over time",[281,306,307,310],{},[284,308,309],{},"Multi-tenancy"," - Built-in tenant isolation at the data layer with shared index support",[281,312,313,316],{},[284,314,315],{},"Named queries"," - Define custom query methods with a SQL-like syntax",[273,318,320],{"id":319},"workflow","Workflow",[269,322,323],{},"The typical workflow for working with Kinotic persistence is:",[325,326,327,336,346],"ol",{},[281,328,329,332,333],{},[284,330,331],{},"Define your entity"," - Create a TypeScript class with decorators from ",[295,334,335],{},"@kinotic-ai\u002Fpersistence",[281,337,338,341,342,345],{},[284,339,340],{},"Sync to server"," - Run ",[295,343,344],{},"kinotic sync"," to push your entity definitions to the Kinotic server and generate typed service classes",[281,347,348,351],{},[284,349,350],{},"Use in your app"," - Import and use the generated services to perform data operations",[273,353,355],{"id":354},"packages","Packages",[269,357,358],{},"Two packages work together to provide the persistence layer:",[278,360,361,381],{},[281,362,363,367,368,371,372,371,375,371,378,380],{},[284,364,365],{},[295,366,335],{}," - Provides entity decorators (",[295,369,370],{},"@Entity",", ",[295,373,374],{},"@AutoGeneratedId",[295,376,377],{},"@NotNull",[295,379,297],{},", etc.), entity service interfaces, and the persistence plugin",[281,382,383,388,389,392],{},[284,384,385],{},[295,386,387],{},"@kinotic-ai\u002Fcore"," - Provides the connection layer (",[295,390,391],{},"Kinotic.connect()","), pagination types, and core utilities shared across all Kinotic packages",{"title":394,"searchDepth":395,"depth":395,"links":396},"",2,[397,398,399],{"id":275,"depth":395,"text":276},{"id":319,"depth":395,"text":320},{"id":354,"depth":395,"text":355},"Kinotic's persistence layer provides declarative data management with automatic CRUD service generation from TypeScript entity definitions.","md",null,{},true,{"title":26,"description":400},"g8NUkMC0tuV7NialQA4y8KUJpDwirmLhankBQvKHAX8",[408,410],{"title":84,"path":85,"stem":86,"description":409,"children":-1},"How a Java program outside a Kinotic cluster connects to a gateway and calls services through typed proxies.",{"title":97,"path":98,"stem":99,"description":411,"children":-1},"How to define entities using TypeScript decorators for Kinotic's persistence layer.",1794209426357]